# rule.always.absorb-every-concern

> **you have not absorbed a reviewer's feedback until you absorb EACH concern within it: one disposition per concern, disputed or conceded, or the road does not pass.**

concern = one blocker or nitpick a reviewer enumerated. law: `define.invariant.review.peer.absorb`. the `.taken` (absorb the feedback) is REFUSED until each concern within it is absorbed.

`conceded` (default): fix it, run again. `disputed` (escalation): shed from tally, council rules, fulcrum `--why` required.

```
rhx route.stone.set --stone <s> --as conceded --with <reviewer> --about <concern> --severity better|urgent
rhx route.stone.set --stone <s> --as disputed  --with <reviewer> --about <concern> --why <fulcrum-path>
```

`--about` names ONE concern by ordinal (`blocker.3`); no `--about all`. ordinals renumber each generation.

| when… | then… |
|---|---|
| a given rejects | each enumerated concern owes an absorption |
| you would write the `.taken` for the reviewer "as a whole" | absorb each concern first |
| you fix the code and re-arrive | a fix is not an absorption; declare on the concern |
| an approved lane's nitpick pushes the stone over the floor | you MAY absorb it (tally is stone-wide) |

test: **for every concern enumerated, did you render a disposition on THAT concern?**
boundary: a concern with no hold owes none (forgiven level, silent lane, unreadable given → re-run).

blocker: passage sought with an un-absorbed counted concern · a code fix re-arrived as a discharge · a disposition on the reviewer as a whole · a dispute with no fulcrum `--why`.
